cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "metrology-atlas: a machine-readable metrology of a recorded dataset"
version: 0.3.0
authors:
  - family-names: Goodwin
    given-names: "Andrew J."
    affiliation: "School of Biomedical Engineering, The University of Sydney"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2776-7039"
abstract: "Describes a recorded dataset as a measurement system, in the terms of the VIM and the GUM: for every variable, the interval each value describes, the bias and standard uncertainty of its time and value, which errors are shared with other signals, how it relates to other variables (what it measures and what it was derived from, with uncertainty and availability propagated along each link), and the evidence behind each number. A schema and engine check an atlas and compile it to one JSON file and a website. Includes the VitalDB atlas (v0.2.0) as its first dataset."
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/metrology-atlas/metrology-atlas"
url: "https://vitaldb.metrology-atlas.org"
keywords:
  - "metrology"
  - "measurement uncertainty"
  - "physiological signals"
  - "clock synchronisation"
  - "data quality"
  - "VitalDB"
